      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WARATAH WHO (5) was prominent early from the tricky draw and did a fair job to be beaten 2 lengths into third (20.15) at this track in a Grade 6 over 342m. Expected to feature in the finish again. ZINFANDEL PEARL (1) was in the money again last time and not beaten far when third (20.11) at this track in a Grade 6. Can find the frame this time. JUNO USKO (7) struggled in tougher grade last start at this track, but prior to that won by a neck at this track (19.89) beating Skate In Paris in a Grade 6 on August 20. Leading chance. SOUTHLINE (8) was strongly fancied last time but finished third (17.36), beaten 6 lengths. Some good form is emerging from his last run. Overdue and expected to feature again.",
